  "id": "final-common-path",
  "term": "final common path",
  "definition": "In this context, the final common path is the shared downstream part of brain reward circuitry where different neural routes converge to support evaluating rewards and pursuing them. The article describes dopamine neurons and non-dopaminergic medial forebrain bundle pathways as parallel inputs that ultimately meet in this common reward-seeking pathway.",
